      "targeted_symptom": "S002",
      "patient_response": "Hi, yeah, nice to meet you too. Um, what brings me in... well, honestly, it's work. I just can't keep my mind on a task long enough to finish it anymore, even when it's really important. Like, I'm a computer support specialist, right? So I'll start tracing a client's network problem, and... you know, networks have gotten so complicated lately. Back when I started, we were dealing with basic token ring setups, but now everything is cloud-based and hybrid, and the documentation vendors provide is just garbage. I mean, absolute garbage. I had this one guy from Cisco try to explain their new licensing model to me last week, and I swear he didn't even understand it himself. He kept talking about... oh, right, sorry. The problem is, I'll be looking at the network issue, and ten minutes later I realize I've reread the same log entries three times and I still have no idea what they actually say. It's just... it's really getting bad.",
